%erg v1
Title: add per-project max_turns_pick_ticket to ProjectConfig (analogous to raid_timeout_s)
Created: 2026-05-10
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-10T21:05Z claude created — nightbeat-supervisor root-cause chain: chemin-de-voix pick_ticket outcome=fail at 19:05Z due to max-turns (30) reached during exit-criteria check for ticket 0071. No per-project knob exists; module-level constant is off-limits. Fix: add configurable field.

--- body ---
## Root cause chain

1. chemin-de-voix pick_ticket outcome=fail 2026-05-10T19:05Z, cost=$0.21
2. Log: `pick-ticket: max-turns (30) reached — context cap hit`
3. Exit-criteria check for ticket 0071 (step 4) consumed all 30 allowed turns running erg, reading beat-skip, reading ticket body, and running shell checks for file presence
4. `MAX_TURNS_PICK_TICKET = 30` is a module-level constant; per-project `max_turns_pick_ticket` does not exist in `ProjectConfig` or `_PROJ_KEYS`
5. Supervisor authority: no per-project knob → ticket required

## Context

`beat.py` already supports per-project `raid_timeout_s` (analogous cap for the raid phase).
The same pattern applies to pick-ticket: some repos with many tickets or complex exit
criteria need more turns. The module-level constant (`MAX_TURNS_PICK_TICKET = 30`) serves
as the floor/default.

The immediate trigger (ticket 0071) was closed at 2026-05-10T19:30Z; next pick-ticket run
will not hit the same issue. But the structural gap remains.

## Goal

Add `max_turns_pick_ticket: int` to `ProjectConfig`, defaulting to `MAX_TURNS_PICK_TICKET`.
Add `"max_turns_pick_ticket"` to `_PROJ_KEYS` so it's readable from `beat.json` overlays.
Wire it into the `_run_skill()` call at line ~1019 of `beat.py`.

## Exit criteria

- `ProjectConfig` has a `max_turns_pick_ticket: int = MAX_TURNS_PICK_TICKET` field
- `"max_turns_pick_ticket"` is in `_PROJ_KEYS`
- The per-project value is passed as `max_turns=` at line ~1019
- `tests/test_beat.py` covers: default value, JSON overlay round-trip
- `scripts/beat.py` tests pass (`make test` or `uv run pytest tests/test_beat.py`)
